    desc: "60/40 or 50/50 stock-bond allocation",
    Icon: ChartPie,
    content: `**Defensive Investor Portfolio Allocation** (Chapters 1 & 4 of The Intelligent Investor) is the foundation of modern balanced investing.

**Core Rule:** Allocate between 50% and 75% to stocks, and 25% to 50% to bonds. The classic starting point is 60% stocks / 40% bonds.

**Glide-path model:** As you age, reduce stock allocation and increase bonds. Example: Age 30 → 70/30; Age 50 → 60/40; Age 65 → 40/60.

**Real-world use today:**
- The "60/40 portfolio" is the industry standard for pension funds and institutional investors
- Basis of all target-date funds (e.g., 2040 Fund, 2050 Fund)
- Used by robo-advisors (Betterment, INDmoney, Wealthfront) for automated allocation

**Why it works:** Stocks provide growth; bonds provide stability. The combination reduces volatility without sacrificing long-term returns.

**For Indian investors:** Equivalent in Equity Mutual Funds + Debt Funds / PPF / EPF.`
